---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Mental Health Research — JD">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <a href="/projects" class="text-sm text-[var(--color-muted)]">← Back to Projects</a>
  </div>

  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-4">Mental Health Research</h1>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-6">
    <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-medium" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Completed</span>
    <a href="https://github.com/Jagruth07/mental-health-research" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-sm">GitHub →</a>
  </div>

  <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
    An end-to-end evaluation pipeline for a RAG-backed AI mental health chatbot that generates 
    therapeutic responses using Indian mythological stories (Ramayana, Mahabharata) retrieved from 
    a vector database. Evaluates generated responses against psychologist-approved references using 
    BERTScore and ROUGE-L, correlating metrics with human ratings.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Tech Stack</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Python</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Sentence-Transformers</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Qdrant</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">BERTScore</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">ROUGE</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Ollama</span>
      <span class="text-xs px-2 py-1 rounded-full font-mono" style="background-color: var(--color-bg);">Pandas</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Pipeline Overview</h2>
    
    <h3 class="text-base font-medium mb-2">Phase 0 — Data Ingestion</h3>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-4">
      291 Ramayana stories are embedded using sentence-transformers (all-mpnet-base-v2) and loaded 
      into a Qdrant vector database for semantic retrieval.
    </p>

    <h3 class="text-base font-medium mb-2">Phase 1 — Generation</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-[var(--color-muted)] space-y-2 mb-4">
      <li>Embed user question with sentence-transformers</li>
      <li>Retrieve top-3 passages from Qdrant</li>
      <li>Inject passages into a strict prompt that forces Story ID citation</li>
      <li>Generate response via Ollama with Qwen3-8B</li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-base font-medium mb-2">Phase 2 — Evaluation</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside text-[var(--color-muted)] space-y-2">
      <li>BERTScore (roberta-large, layer 17) — semantic similarity</li>
      <li>ROUGE-L — surface-level word overlap</li>
      <li>Correlation analysis with human psychologist ratings</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Key Findings</h2>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      LLM-as-Judge for empathic validation scored 1.000 vs regex at 0.349 — demonstrating that 
      content-based citation analysis reveals retrieval fidelity improvements even when BERTScore drops 
      after switching from loose to strict prompt forcing. The D4 CBT Protocol metric remains a known 
      anomaly requiring backend investigation.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-6">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">Research Context</h2>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed">
      Psychologist references in the evaluation dataset are LLM-generated responses reviewed by 
      psychologists, a known methodological limitation. The work contributes to understanding how 
      culturally-grounded RAG systems can be evaluated for therapeutic content generation using 
      both automated metrics and human judgment.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
